invariant: INV-7
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_open opens a Handshake packet in a version the
  connection did not negotiate, which RFC 9369 section 4.1 makes an
  endpoint drop (rfc9369.txt:256-259). test/quic_version_tests.h opens
  the server's Handshake packet in four other versions and requires
  CH_EINVAL with the packet and the failure count unchanged.

--- old
    if (session_dead(q) || level > CH_LEVEL_APPLICATION || !version_ok(q, level, version) ||
        (q->levels_ready & CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_READ)) == 0) {
--- new
    if (session_dead(q) || level > CH_LEVEL_APPLICATION ||
        (q->levels_ready & CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_READ)) == 0) {
